# The sidecar authenticates nobody by itself. Its upstream must stay on the loopback address and be
# reachable only through the proxy that runs the device-check subrequest. Never forward, bridge or
# expose it on another interface or on the tailnet.
#
# PROPOSAL, not applied. Goes inside the proxy host site block, BEFORE the catch-all
# `handle`. lucina-updates (crates/lucina-updates) serves the signed manifest and the artefacts of each
# product channel, read-only and keyless; a device verifies everything itself, so this block only
# keeps the code private (device auth) and delivers big files cheaply.
#
# The sidecar listens on loopback of the host that runs it (127.0.0.1:8811), not on the tailnet address like
# lucina-media, so the proxy needs a path to it. The way the proxy reaches the sidecar is decided at deploy and must
# keep the sidecar unreachable by anything but the proxy. UPDATES_UPSTREAM below is that address.
@updates path /v1/updates/*
handle @updates {
	route {
		# Read-only: anything but GET and HEAD stops here (the sidecar also answers 405).
		@updates_write not method GET HEAD
		respond @updates_write `{"ok":false,"error":"method_not_allowed"}` 405
		# Same device check as /v1/media, its own rate bucket (secretary-server /v1/auth/updates).
		forward_auth 127.0.0.1:8800 {
			uri /v1/auth/updates
		}
		# Nothing is uploaded here.
		request_body {
			max_size 1KiB
		}
		# UPDATES_UPSTREAM must be replaced by the address at which the proxy reaches the sidecar (it listens on
		# 127.0.0.1:8811 on the host that runs it). The coordinator sets it at deploy; do not apply this snippet while it is undefined.
		reverse_proxy UPDATES_UPSTREAM {
			# Large artefacts and Range requests stream through: no buffering, no read deadline
			# for a slow phone.
			flush_interval -1
			transport http {
				response_header_timeout 30s
				read_timeout 0
				write_timeout 0
			}
			header_up -Authorization
			header_up -Cookie
		}
	}
}
